WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.480
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am&nbsp;
going to explain a drama film called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.560
“Room”. Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:21.360
Twenty-four-year-old Joy lives in a tiny room&nbsp;
with her son Jack. The room has a toilet and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:27.280
bath in one corner and a makeshift kitchen in&nbsp;
the other. The mother and son share a single bed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:32.560
because of the limited space. It has only a&nbsp;
skylight that works as the window and the door&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:38.880
needs a passcode to be opened. Jack has never in&nbsp;
his life been out of the room. His mother Joy was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:45.200
abducted by a man seven years ago who has been&nbsp;
holding her captive in the same room ever since.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:50.400
Jack is the result of the sexual abuse Joy had&nbsp;
to go through because of the abductor. The only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:56.320
form of entertainment the kid has is an old&nbsp;
TV which he thinks is a magic box. He believes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:02.080
that people inside the TV are aliens who live&nbsp;
on another planet with trees and animals. 
&nbsp;

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:07.360
The film begins with Jack waking up and saying&nbsp;
hi to the inanimate objects around the room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:13.760
like the chair, the wardrobe, the sink, and so&nbsp;
on. Since he has only seen two people in his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:19.040
he has made friends with the objects around&nbsp;
the room. The kid has no concept of space and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:25.040
thinks that the room is all that exists. To avoid&nbsp;
explaining the harsh truth of his life, Joy has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:30.960
never told him about the outside world. The two&nbsp;
have named the abductor, “Old Nick”. He comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:37.280
Joy every night and assaults her sexually. After&nbsp;
seven years of torture, she has gotten used to it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.840
He also brings them necessary groceries&nbsp;
and buys them clothes once in a while.
&nbsp;

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.480
Jack is excited because today is his fifth&nbsp;
birthday. His mother makes him a cake with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:51.920
whatever materials they have. Jack is stoked about&nbsp;
getting something he has only ever seen on TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.040
but is disappointed to see the cake has no&nbsp;
candles. He demands that Joy should have asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:03.120
Old Nick for candles for their Sunday treat. Joy&nbsp;
claims she can only ask him for necessary goods.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:08.240
When it turns dark, she makes Jack sleep&nbsp;
inside a tiny cupboard as usual. She does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:13.280
this so the kid wouldn’t have to witness Old Nick&nbsp;
assaulting her. When the abductor enters the room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.520
Jack watches him through the slats of the&nbsp;
cupboard. He is terrified of going out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.640
because he can tell the man hurts his mother. 
The following day, as Joy is eating breakfast, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:29.440
bad tooth falls off her mouth. She hands it to her&nbsp;
son who keeps it in his mouth. They have breakfast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:34.400
which is only a piece of toast. The kid wishes&nbsp;
to eat something else but Joy doesn’t respond,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.320
knowing that this is all she can provide&nbsp;
him. When Jack wakes up the next morning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:43.840
he is overjoyed to see a brand new toy car on&nbsp;
the table. Old Nick has brought it for him as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.640
present for his birthday. Jack believes that&nbsp;
Old Nick is a magician who can bring stuff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:54.240
out of the TV. He plays with the car the entire&nbsp;
day around the room. For an hour or so, the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:59.840
scream at the ceiling, hoping to catch someone’s&nbsp;
attention, but as usual, nothing happens. 
&nbsp;

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:05.520
Later while talking, Jack mentions his imaginary&nbsp;
pet dog Lucky. Joy tells him that Lucky isn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:11.280
real, making him upset. When Joy is distracted,&nbsp;
Jack sees a mouse on the floor for the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:17.200
time in his life. He tries to touch it but Joy&nbsp;
notices and chases it away. He is sad because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.640
the mouse was the only animal he has ever seen.&nbsp;
That night, while making dinner, Joy accidentally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:27.360
leaves the toaster oven on and it catches&nbsp;
on fire. She quickly turns it off and tries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:32.720
to wave off the smell, hoping Old Nick wouldn’t&nbsp;
notice. However, when he comes around at night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:38.240
he smells the burnt cheese instantly. He gets&nbsp;
annoyed and calls her names. When she snaps back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:43.760
with a snarky comment, he gets violently angry&nbsp;
and almost hits her. It turns out that he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:49.200
laid off from work six months ago, and can hardly&nbsp;
provide for the three of them. Poor Jack tries to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:54.640
ignore the conversation but accidentally makes&nbsp;
a noise. Old Nick notices and tries to open the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.640 --> 00:04:00.160
cupboard to see him. To keep him from talking&nbsp;
to her son, Joy invites him to the bed. 
&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.440
Later that night, Jack sneaks out of his cupboard&nbsp;
and tiptoes over to the two of them. Old Nick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:11.280
happens to be awake and sees the kid. He lunges&nbsp;
for Jack but Joy throws herself on top of him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:17.440
preventing him from touching her son. An enraged&nbsp;
Nick threatens to kill her and storms off leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:23.440
a crying Jack behind. Joy consoles him as he&nbsp;
sobs in her arms and apologizes for coming out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:28.480
of the cupboard. The next morning, the room&nbsp;
is suspiciously cold. Joy notices that their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:33.280
heater is turned off which means Old Nick must&nbsp;
have cut off the power supply to the shed. 
&nbsp;

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:38.240
Joy knows that they cannot survive in the cold&nbsp;
for long. Moreover, with the shortage of money,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:44.000
she is afraid Nick will starve them to death. So,&nbsp;
she sits Jack down and explains to him that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:49.440
are being held in a shed by a bad person.&nbsp;
She tells him that she was only seventeen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:55.600
when Old Nick asked her to help him with his sick&nbsp;
dog. He fooled her and kidnapped her in the shed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.760
Before that, she used to live with Jack’s&nbsp;
grandparents in a house that had a hammock.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:05.520
The kid refuses to believe her and declares that&nbsp;
trees, houses, and hammocks only exist on TV.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:10.000
Although Jack is stubborn, Joy keeps on&nbsp;
telling him things about the outside world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.960
She even shows him a dried leaf that has fallen&nbsp;
on the skylight but the kid insists the leaves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:19.360
are green so she must be lying. 
The next day, while watching TV,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:24.080
he asks her if trees and people are really&nbsp;
real. Joy calmly explains to him how the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.480
real world works, finally making him&nbsp;
believe her. Not wasting much time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:34.720
she devises a plan to escape. She boils water and&nbsp;
uses it to make it look like Jack has a fever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:39.680
She even forces herself to vomit and spreads&nbsp;
it around the pillow to make him smell bad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:44.560
The kid cries and claims he doesn’t want to&nbsp;
do it. Joy doesn’t enjoy seeing him crying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:49.760
but she has no other way to escape. When Old Nick&nbsp;
arrives that night, she tells him that the cold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:54.880
has made Jack sick. Nick touches his forehead&nbsp;
which is burning because of the hot water. 
&nbsp;

00:05:54.880 --> 00:06:00.480
He claims that he will bring antibiotics the next&nbsp;
day and leaves. Joy is disappointed because she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:04.800
had thought he would take Jack to the hospital&nbsp;
where the kid would have a chance to escape. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:11.360
following day, she thinks of a new plan. She&nbsp;
asks Jack to pretend to be dead and rolls him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:17.840
in a rug. She trains him to unroll himself and run&nbsp;
for help. The kid is told he will be taken outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:24.400
by Old Nick where he will meet real people who&nbsp;
he has to ask for help. He is scared but agrees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:30.560
to do it. When Old Nick arrives a while later,&nbsp;
Joy has already wrapped up Jack inside the rug&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:35.840
and is pretending to cry. She claims that he&nbsp;
died during the night and blames Old Nick for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:42.160
his death. Nick panics and quickly brings the kid&nbsp;
out, still rolled up in the rug. He puts him into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:48.240
the back of a pickup truck and drives off. From&nbsp;
inside the rug, Jack feels the truck driving. 
&nbsp;

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:54.480
He unravels from the rug and is mesmerized to see&nbsp;
the full view of the sky for the first time. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:59.520
the truck slows down, he carefully jumps out&nbsp;
of it. Old Nick notices and stops the truck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:05.200
but by then, Jack has already met a man walking&nbsp;
his dog. Old Nick tries to bring Jack back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:10.960
the vehicle but the man finds it suspicious and&nbsp;
threatens to call the police. Old Nick drives away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:15.920
after leaving the kid lying on the ground.&nbsp;
Jack stays there until he is rescued by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:20.240
police. He tells them about his mother&nbsp;
and shows them the tooth he has of her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.560
When he mentions that they live in a shed that&nbsp;
they aren’t allowed to leave, the police realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:30.160
the severity of the situation. They quickly call&nbsp;
for backup and start searching for the shed. 
&nbsp;

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:35.520
Only some hours later, they rescue Joy who&nbsp;
is fortunately safe. She reunites with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:41.200
son and praises him for his work. The two hug,&nbsp;
celebrating their freedom after being captured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:47.280
for seven years. When Jack wakes up the next day,&nbsp;
he finds himself in a bed in a hospital room. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:53.120
looks outside the window, still unable to believe&nbsp;
that the outside world is real. Joy and he takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:58.560
a bath in a shower for the first time. Jack is&nbsp;
scared to go under running water but eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:04.080
gets used to it. The doctors perform several&nbsp;
tests on them and declare them healthy. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:09.760
are suggested to wear a lot of sunscreens since&nbsp;
they were hardly exposed to sunlight in captivity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:15.600
Jack is also told to wear sunglasses if the world&nbsp;
seems too bright. The kid is nervous to talk to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:21.840
the doctor so he quietly whispers to Joy if he&nbsp;
wants to say something. Joy’s parents Nancy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:28.080
Robert finally arrive at the hospital and embrace&nbsp;
their long-lost daughter in a tight hug. They had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:33.200
accepted she was never going to return after&nbsp;
suddenly disappearing one day. Joy is told that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:39.120
her parents have divorced and her mother is now&nbsp;
dating a man named Leo. Following that, Joy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:44.640
Jack are taken home where a crowd of people and&nbsp;
reporters have gathered to witness the return. 
&nbsp;

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:50.720
Jack needs help to walk down the stairs because he&nbsp;
is not used to it. He meets Leo who is delighted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:55.680
to see both of them. After they are settled, Nancy&nbsp;
comments that they should cut Jack’s hair but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:01.280
kid quietly whispers that his strength is in his&nbsp;
hair. At dinner, the family enjoys a nutritious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:07.360
meal that is foreign for Jack. He eats ice cream&nbsp;
for the first time and experiences a brain freeze.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:15.920
Joy notices that her father hasn’t talked to Jack&nbsp;
at all. She realizes that he is not comfortable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:20.960
with Jack being his grandchild because he was&nbsp;
the product of her being sexually assaulted.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:25.360
Enraged that he is not willing to accept&nbsp;
her son, she gets into an argument with him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:30.320
and storms off to her room with Jack. 
The next day, Joy shows Jack a picture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:34.560
of her and her high school friends. She is&nbsp;
clearly annoyed at the fact that their lives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:39.920
turned out to be nice when she was rotting&nbsp;
in the hell of a room. Jack has a hard time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:45.040
adjusting to the new life. He never leaves his&nbsp;
mother's side and doesn’t talk to anyone else.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:50.160
Leo makes the kid comfortable and talks to him&nbsp;
like a father which helps him a lot. Joy falls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:55.120
deep into depression after failing to be&nbsp;
happy even after getting out of captivity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.120 --> 00:10:00.320
She forces Jack to play even when he refuses&nbsp;
to and gets into a huge argument with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:05.360
mother. Some days later, their family's lawyer&nbsp;
informs them that they will need money for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:10.160
upcoming trial, and the easiest way to get&nbsp;
some is to do a prime-time interview.
&nbsp;

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:15.520
A journalist shows up at the house to interview&nbsp;
Joy. She asks her intrusive questions about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:20.880
self-harm and her relationship with the captor,&nbsp;
making her feel worse than she already did.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:26.080
At one point in the interview, Joy is asked why&nbsp;
she didn’t beg the abductor to leave Jack in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:32.160
orphanage, implying that she was selfish. The&nbsp;
interview has upset her so much that she sinks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:37.840
into depression. The next morning Jack walks to&nbsp;
the bathroom and is horrified to see his mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:41.440
laying on the ground. Joy has attempted to commit&nbsp;
suicide but she is soon saved by the paramedics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:46.800
While Joy is admitted to the hospital, Jack&nbsp;
is left alone with Nancy and Leo. With time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:51.760
he begins opening up to them and gets used&nbsp;
to being around people. Leo brings his dog&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:58.000
home which excites Jack, who still remembers&nbsp;
his imaginary dog, Lucky. One day, Jack tells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:03.840
Nancy he wants to cut his hair and send it to Joy&nbsp;
because she needs his strength more than he does.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:09.120
Nancy happily does as he says and gives the boy&nbsp;
a neat haircut. At the end of it, the kid tells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:14.720
her that he loves her. Nancy is overwhelmed and&nbsp;
hardly manages to whisper back I love you. 
&nbsp;

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:21.200
That day, a neighbor's kid calls Jack out to play.&nbsp;
He makes a friend for the first time in his life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:27.040
and plays with him in the backyard. At the same&nbsp;
time, Joy returns home and smiles while watching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:32.720
him play. When the mother and the son meet, she&nbsp;
claims that his hair helped her get well quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:38.400
As time passes, Jack experiences several things&nbsp;
with his mother. They go to different restaurants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:43.760
parks, and places that they didn’t get to visit&nbsp;
for all those years. They also hang a hammock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:48.320
at the house that Jack had always wanted&nbsp;
to play in. As the two are swinging in it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:54.320
Jack asks to visit the room once. Joy is shocked&nbsp;
at the request but she agrees to take him for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.320 --> 00:12:00.320
visit. When Jack returns to the place, he comments&nbsp;
if it has shrunk since they were last here because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:06.640
he remembers it being bigger. Before leaving, he&nbsp;
wishes the objects in the room a goodbye like he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:11.680
used to wish them while in captivity. 
